# Clean Code Checklist

- Keep functions focused on one responsibility.
- Extract duplicated behavior into reusable units.
- Validate inputs at system boundaries and fail fast.
- Use descriptive names for symbols and types.
- Prefer self-documenting code; comments should explain business intent.
- Keep formatting and grouping consistent.

## Before Finishing

- Changed functions remain small and readable.
- New logic is covered by tests when behavior changes.
- Comments explain why, not what.
